Hi @salmanahmedtamu

I rechecked duplicated records by creating dummy column which is concatenation of all the columns.

train_ss_labels["dummy"] = (
    train_ss_labels["filename"] + "_" +
    train_ss_labels["start"] + "_" +
    train_ss_labels["end"] + "_" +
    train_ss_labels["primary_label"]
)
print(train_ss_labels.groupby("dummy")["filename"].count().value_counts())
# ↓
# filename
# 2    739
# Name: count, dtype: int64
After all, I think there are two identical records for each 739 data point.


